/// A program whose entry point fails has to say so, and exit non-zero.
///
/// `instance.Run();` discarded the result, so a `?` propagating out of the entry point ended the
/// program **silently with status 0**: the output simply stopped halfway and a shell, a CI job or
/// an agent running the binary read that as success. The expected output below ends before the
/// failure on purpose, and `expected/entry_failure_exits.exit` pins the status.
agent Main {
    public void Run() {
        print "this line runs";
        var n = parse_int("not-a-number")?;
        print "this line must not appear";
    }
}
